WEBVTT

00:00.020 --> 00:03.770
OP (V1)

01:18.180 --> 01:20.930
Presented by QuinRose.

01:49.500 --> 01:50.840
Stop right there!

01:50.840 --> 01:53.920
You say stop, but you think we will?

01:53.920 --> 01:56.720
Come and catch us, faceless!

01:59.430 --> 02:02.560
But... I want us to stop, too!

02:06.390 --> 02:08.770
Say, did you know...

02:08.770 --> 02:11.400
that every game has rules?

02:11.940 --> 02:14.150
Rules that are meant to be broken.

02:14.860 --> 02:18.820
There are rules for those
who don't play the game, too.

02:18.820 --> 02:23.160
I await your participation. You can't refuse.

02:25.660 --> 02:28.960
So... let the game begin.

02:33.630 --> 02:34.710
Alice...

02:39.380 --> 02:42.260
Did you have a nice nap, Alice?

02:43.180 --> 02:45.560
I had a very strange dream.

02:45.560 --> 02:46.640
A dream?

02:47.930 --> 02:49.100
About what?

02:50.310 --> 02:52.810
I don't really remember.

02:52.810 --> 02:55.570
Something about a game and rules...

02:55.570 --> 02:56.400
A game?

02:56.400 --> 02:58.110
You played a game?

02:58.740 --> 03:00.610
Not exactly...

03:00.610 --> 03:02.240
It was just in my dream.

03:02.240 --> 03:05.240
Dreams are reflections of your true desires.

03:05.240 --> 03:08.000
You must have wanted to play a game, Alice.

03:08.000 --> 03:09.250
That's not it.

03:09.250 --> 03:11.870
They were telling me about a game...

03:11.870 --> 03:12.750
Don't worry!

03:12.750 --> 03:15.090
You must want to play a game.

03:15.090 --> 03:16.800
Don't tell me otherwise.

03:16.800 --> 03:18.050
I'm not...

03:19.630 --> 03:22.550
I'll bring something out.
What would you like to play?

03:22.550 --> 03:24.510
I don't want to play! Nee-san!

03:24.510 --> 03:26.600
If you're tired of board games,

03:26.600 --> 03:29.020
maybe you would like a card game.

03:29.020 --> 03:30.100
Nee-san!

03:31.770 --> 03:35.820
Cards... are so simple!

03:49.290 --> 03:52.750
Catch them! If you can't, then kill them!

03:54.630 --> 03:59.380
Geez! You're so stubborn!
You guys should give up!

04:04.180 --> 04:05.760
Let's go, Onee-san!

04:05.260 --> 04:06.850
Wait!

04:06.850 --> 04:10.430
You shouldn't chase after women and children!

04:10.430 --> 04:13.060
But I guess that's how you play tag!

04:13.060 --> 04:15.690
H-How is this playing tag?!

04:17.940 --> 04:18.900
Huh?

04:19.730 --> 04:21.820
What's up, Onee-san?

04:21.820 --> 04:24.360
Shouldn't we be at the ball?

04:24.360 --> 04:28.660
If there's no one around,
we aren't going to get any help.

04:29.290 --> 04:34.040
Is there a shortcut? I didn't think
they would go so out of their way.

04:34.790 --> 04:38.920
Before we go, we have a present for you.

04:38.920 --> 04:41.340
Yes, a present! We're going to entertain you!

04:41.340 --> 04:42.090
Huh?

04:43.220 --> 04:45.090
Look, Onee-san!

04:54.890 --> 04:58.150
I knew I would find you here.

04:58.900 --> 05:00.780
Don't say something so stupid!

05:00.780 --> 05:01.900
I forgot.

05:01.900 --> 05:04.610
You never were like anyone else, were you...

05:04.610 --> 05:06.070
Bloody Twins?

05:06.570 --> 05:11.120
Well, everyone is at the ball,
so no one can help you.

05:11.120 --> 05:12.500
Anyway,

05:12.500 --> 05:16.500
what were you trying to
accomplish by leading us here?

05:16.500 --> 05:18.000
Let's play tag.

05:18.000 --> 05:18.790
Huh?

05:18.830 --> 05:22.300
Let's play tag. I want to play.

05:22.300 --> 05:24.630
D-Don't screw around!

05:24.630 --> 05:28.090
We were told that we have to
capture the three of you!

05:28.090 --> 05:29.300
He's "it".

05:29.300 --> 05:31.100
Let's go, Onee-san.

05:31.100 --> 05:32.220
W-Wai...

05:35.230 --> 05:36.060
Stop!

05:36.060 --> 05:37.100
Come here!

05:49.070 --> 05:51.120
I... I can't go on...

05:51.120 --> 05:53.120
You must, Onee-san.

05:54.580 --> 05:55.910
Yes. You must.

05:57.370 --> 05:59.000
One, two.

05:59.380 --> 06:01.090
Don't worry, Onee-san.

06:01.090 --> 06:04.420
We're grown-ups, so we won't give up that easily.

06:04.420 --> 06:06.720
Wh-What does that mean?

06:06.720 --> 06:11.180
Even adults would have given up
by now! Why don't you?

06:11.680 --> 06:13.600
It's all right, Onee-san.

06:13.600 --> 06:16.310
I-I-It's not all right!

06:21.690 --> 06:24.780
I'm gonna die! I'm gonna die!

06:24.780 --> 06:26.610
I won't let you die!

06:26.610 --> 06:29.200
I <i>will</i> die! We're falling!

06:29.200 --> 06:34.160
Indeed we are falling. We're in a hole,
so falling is to be expected.

06:34.160 --> 06:38.910
Why is this hole even here?!
How did it get here?! Where's my sister?!

06:38.910 --> 06:42.630
You needn't ask irrelevant questions like "where" and "why".

06:42.630 --> 06:45.170
Those are important questions, not irrelevant!

06:45.170 --> 06:47.720
We're falling into a gigantic hole!

06:47.720 --> 06:50.430
And I'm being kidnapped! By a pervert!

06:52.640 --> 06:54.600
I am not a pervert.

06:54.600 --> 06:56.470
I am Peter White.

06:57.020 --> 06:58.930
Peter White?

06:58.930 --> 06:59.730
Yes.

07:04.730 --> 07:06.530
Please call me Peter.

07:25.960 --> 07:26.920
You...!

07:26.920 --> 07:29.760
I am not "You". I'm Peter.

07:29.760 --> 07:31.050
Peter?

07:31.050 --> 07:33.340
Yes! Peter White.

07:33.340 --> 07:36.260
I am the rabbit who's in love with you!

07:38.180 --> 07:40.180
Peter White...

07:40.180 --> 07:42.650
Yes, Alice? What can I do?

07:42.650 --> 07:44.730
You suddenly kissed me...

07:44.730 --> 07:46.940
Because I love you, of course.

07:46.940 --> 07:49.440
Oh, but that was a bit messy.

07:49.440 --> 07:51.070
Messy?

07:51.070 --> 07:53.450
Yes, with your saliva.

07:53.450 --> 07:56.830
S-Saliva? <i>You</i> came onto <i>me</i>.

07:56.830 --> 08:01.540
Yes, but if I get to kiss you, then a mess is no problem.

08:01.540 --> 08:03.790
And I had to make you drink the potion.

08:03.790 --> 08:06.290
Making me drink a strange potion...

08:06.290 --> 08:08.000
How could you?

08:08.000 --> 08:09.960
Peter White...

08:09.960 --> 08:11.470
I'll kill you!

09:11.150 --> 09:13.150
What? It couldn't be!

09:24.620 --> 09:27.040
This is where the White Rabbit's hole ended.

09:27.670 --> 09:30.920
I'm now living in a bizarre world

09:31.340 --> 09:35.720
where life is meaningless and hails of bullets are everywhere.

09:36.430 --> 09:41.180
The inhabitants are divided into "the faceless" and "the role holders".

09:41.600 --> 09:46.480
The faceless are just cards compared to the courts of the role holders.

09:47.190 --> 09:48.520
The Castle of Hearts,

09:51.900 --> 09:54.690
and the Queen of Hearts, Vivaldi.

09:54.690 --> 09:57.700
A dangerous woman who likes to have people's heads cut off.

09:57.700 --> 10:01.660
You get no trial! Off with his head!

10:01.660 --> 10:03.740
I-Is that not a tad...

10:05.960 --> 10:09.580
The one who brought me here, the White Rabbit.

10:09.580 --> 10:13.130
If you can't even resolve such a trivial dispute,

10:13.130 --> 10:15.550
your service is not needed here.

10:15.550 --> 10:20.680
He is cold to everyone but me—the Prime Minister, Peter White.

10:23.140 --> 10:25.600
The Knave of Hearts, Ace.

10:26.060 --> 10:30.810
He's got no sense of direction. He even gets lost in the castle he lives in.

10:31.400 --> 10:35.280
Ace-sama, if you start fires in the corridor, then it will spread...

10:35.280 --> 10:36.610
Huh? What was that?

10:36.610 --> 10:40.200
You want some, too? You're pretty cheeky for a faceless!

10:47.580 --> 10:48.750
The Amusement Park,

10:49.290 --> 10:52.290
and its owner, Mary Gowland.

10:52.290 --> 10:55.630
A man who likes to make awful music.

10:58.340 --> 11:04.100
Yet he is as powerful as those of the Castle of Hearts or the Hatter's Mansion.

11:09.310 --> 11:11.730
The Cheshire Cat, Boris Airay.

11:11.730 --> 11:13.940
An avid lover of riddles.

11:16.030 --> 11:20.150
My Kalashnikov automatic—AK-47.

11:20.150 --> 11:23.910
Ah, banana magazines are the best.

11:23.910 --> 11:26.330
He's a real weapon geek, despite his looks.

11:30.500 --> 11:31.830
The Clock Tower,

11:32.420 --> 11:34.630
and the watchmaker, Julius Monrey.

11:35.210 --> 11:39.420
He can be cold and rude, but he is kind.

11:43.340 --> 11:45.640
Lastly, the Hatter's Mansion,

11:48.520 --> 11:51.270
and the Hatter, Blood Dupre.

11:51.270 --> 11:53.730
A selfish and egocentric man.

11:57.230 --> 12:00.280
The March Hare, Elliot March.

12:00.570 --> 12:04.070
Blood's confidant, loyal and temperamental.

12:04.070 --> 12:06.490
A hare who could fire his gun at any moment.

12:09.240 --> 12:11.040
Tweedle Dee and Dum.

12:11.040 --> 12:15.040
The gatekeepers who love sleeping, money, and armed combat.

12:16.340 --> 12:18.550
We need to kill the bad guys!

12:18.550 --> 12:20.670
'Cause we're good boys!

12:24.010 --> 12:26.850
It's an unusual world with unusual people.

12:26.850 --> 12:31.730
For now, I'm staying in the Hatter's Mansion, the strangest of them all.

12:32.270 --> 12:35.560
It's the most dangerous, but I'm getting used to it.

12:38.730 --> 12:41.650
At least I thought I was, but...

12:42.610 --> 12:44.700
We're falling! We're gonna die!

12:44.700 --> 12:47.990
Die! Die! Die! We're gonna die—!

12:47.990 --> 12:51.290
We're not going to die! It's all right, Onee-san!

12:51.290 --> 12:52.910
He's right. Just calm down.

12:52.910 --> 12:54.620
How can you expect me to calm down?!

12:54.620 --> 12:55.920
Because we're fine!

13:00.840 --> 13:02.550
W-Wait!

13:15.940 --> 13:17.980
See? I told you it's all right.

13:17.980 --> 13:20.520
We'll protect you, so no need to worry.

13:21.900 --> 13:24.030
It's not all right!

13:24.030 --> 13:27.360
It's <i>your</i> fault we got into this!

13:37.420 --> 13:42.380
fukai yami ochiteikeba chigau sekai

13:37.420 --> 13:42.380
If you fall into the darkness, you'll end up in another world

13:42.380 --> 13:47.630
miruku iro kiri no naka ni yobareteru ki ga suru

13:42.380 --> 13:47.630
You'll feel as though the milky-white mist is calling to you

13:47.630 --> 13:52.850
dare no mono? mekki ga hage iro aseteku

13:47.630 --> 13:52.850
Whose is this? Break the façade and fade away

13:52.850 --> 13:58.440
watashi nara takaramono wa dare nimo yuzuranai

13:52.850 --> 13:58.440
I won't give my treasure to anyone

13:58.810 --> 14:03.900
garasu no kutsu wo migaite mo muda ne

13:58.810 --> 14:03.900
Don't bother polishing your glass slippers

14:03.900 --> 14:09.740
oujisama wa koko niwa konai

14:03.900 --> 14:09.740
No prince will come for you here

14:10.530 --> 14:13.490
Bullets

14:11.530 --> 14:14.500
fly in

14:12.530 --> 14:15.500
the Red World

14:12.530 --> 14:15.500
Wonderworld

14:13.540 --> 14:15.870
If your
heart

14:14.540 --> 14:15.870
is lost,

14:15.870 --> 14:16.620
you can never return.

14:16.410 --> 14:20.000
ochiteyuku dake no wandawarudo

14:16.410 --> 14:20.170
A wonderworld where all you do is fall

14:20.000 --> 14:23.880
wasurerareteku yuuenchi

14:20.170 --> 14:24.090
The amusement park you'll soon forget

14:23.880 --> 14:26.550
kirei na mono wa yume

14:24.090 --> 14:26.670
Everything beautiful is a dream

14:26.550 --> 14:31.510
biizu no yubiwa wa itsuka wa chigireru

14:26.670 --> 14:31.680
The bead ring will eventually be torn apart

14:31.510 --> 14:38.020
watashi no omocha yo kodomo no mama isasete

14:31.680 --> 14:38.020
With all my toys, just let me stay a child

14:38.020 --> 14:43.190
torokeru wana ni deguchi ga mienai

14:38.020 --> 14:43.400
It's an enchanting trap with no escape in sight

14:43.400 --> 14:48.360
usagi ga warau wandarando

14:43.400 --> 14:48.360
Where the rabbit laughs—Wonderland

15:02.630 --> 15:03.630
Wait!

15:03.630 --> 15:05.420
Peter, wait!

15:07.300 --> 15:08.420
Hurry!

15:08.970 --> 15:09.970
C'mon, faster! Go faster!

15:09.970 --> 15:10.510
Faster, faster, faster!

15:10.510 --> 15:11.340
Hurry up!

15:11.340 --> 15:11.760
Faster!

15:12.010 --> 15:13.390
Hurry!

15:12.430 --> 15:14.180
Hurry up!

15:17.930 --> 15:18.930
Hurry up!

15:18.930 --> 15:19.730
Hurry!

15:19.230 --> 15:21.150
You'll be late!

15:19.730 --> 15:21.150
Hold on!

15:21.150 --> 15:21.850
I am...

15:30.280 --> 15:31.530
Ugh...

15:33.660 --> 15:35.280
Nightmare!

15:35.280 --> 15:39.160
Where were you in a hurry to, Alice?

15:39.160 --> 15:40.710
Where?

15:40.710 --> 15:42.920
To hurry and wake up.

15:42.920 --> 15:44.330
Why?

15:44.330 --> 15:46.710
Because this is a dream!

15:46.710 --> 15:48.760
It can't be real!

15:49.170 --> 15:50.920
You're right.

15:50.920 --> 15:52.840
This world is a dream,

15:53.180 --> 15:55.800
so you have no reason to hurry.

15:55.800 --> 15:58.270
But I have to go home!

15:58.270 --> 16:00.100
Wasn't this a dream?

16:00.100 --> 16:02.520
You needn't leave.

16:02.520 --> 16:04.560
Your home is right there, after all.

16:04.560 --> 16:06.610
Take your time.

16:11.200 --> 16:12.490
Stop that!

16:14.700 --> 16:16.490
Now, over here!

16:38.680 --> 16:39.850
Blood?

16:40.470 --> 16:41.480
Alice.

16:53.360 --> 16:54.610
Nee-san!

17:14.680 --> 17:15.930
Over here!

17:17.930 --> 17:20.100
This way, Alice.

17:20.100 --> 17:22.470
You will be happy here.

17:23.430 --> 17:25.520
I'll be happy there?

17:25.520 --> 17:27.770
Yes, I shall take you...

17:27.770 --> 17:30.400
to a world of happiness for you.

17:39.830 --> 17:42.160
All will stop for you.

17:42.620 --> 17:45.580
Stop, for <i>you!</i>

18:08.980 --> 18:11.190
We weren't gonna hold up the ball!

18:11.190 --> 18:12.440
Yeah!

18:12.440 --> 18:15.070
We really weren't gonna!

18:15.070 --> 18:20.120
Even so, it's your fault. We had to delay the ball's opening.

18:21.240 --> 18:26.870
It was stupid to even ask them to escort Alice here, wasn't it, Number Two?

18:26.870 --> 18:28.540
I had no choice!

18:28.540 --> 18:30.540
We've been busy lately.

18:30.540 --> 18:32.340
We didn't have people to spare.

18:32.340 --> 18:33.750
Right, Blood?

18:33.750 --> 18:34.710
Absolutely.

18:34.710 --> 18:38.510
But adults have things to do, Little Ones.

18:41.890 --> 18:44.810
I'd have gladly escorted her if you asked me.

18:47.640 --> 18:50.270
I wouldn't have let you get hurt. Are you okay?

18:51.020 --> 18:53.650
Well, at least I'm not dead.

18:53.650 --> 18:56.280
What?! Mind your own business, Boris!

18:56.280 --> 18:57.740
You're just a damn cat!

18:57.740 --> 18:59.240
And the two of you

18:59.240 --> 19:01.570
are just children, yet so vulgar.

19:02.950 --> 19:07.830
You're from the Mafia, yet you play tag all the way to the castle.

19:07.830 --> 19:10.330
Even on the day of the ball.

19:10.670 --> 19:14.540
If it weren't for the Cat, your heads would surely be rolling.

19:14.540 --> 19:17.710
Hold on, Your Majesty, calm down.

19:17.710 --> 19:18.970
You're correct.

19:18.970 --> 19:21.090
The Cat earns you our forgiveness.

19:26.390 --> 19:29.270
Come, Cat, were you not hungry?

19:29.270 --> 19:30.850
Have as much as you would like.

19:30.850 --> 19:36.070
N-No, see, I <i>am</i> a cat, but I'm a Cheshire cat, so I don't eat cat food...

19:36.070 --> 19:38.400
Come! Come, come!

19:38.780 --> 19:41.780
But I don't want to eat it...

19:43.870 --> 19:45.870
Do not be reserved, Cat.

19:45.870 --> 19:47.740
There is still much more to eat!

19:47.740 --> 19:48.700
Ack!

19:49.910 --> 19:51.710
We're sorry, Onee-san.

19:51.710 --> 19:52.830
Are you mad?

19:52.830 --> 19:55.130
Yes. What if I got killed?

19:55.130 --> 19:58.000
We didn't want you to get killed.

19:58.000 --> 20:00.260
I was still scared!

20:00.260 --> 20:01.590
I guess...

20:01.590 --> 20:03.720
You're irreplaceable.

20:05.220 --> 20:07.850
You two are irreplaceable as well.

20:07.850 --> 20:09.470
Can you forgive us?

20:09.470 --> 20:12.270
Of course! Just don't be so reckless again.

20:12.270 --> 20:13.520
Oh, good!

20:13.520 --> 20:18.780
You looked depressed, so we wanted to cheer you up, not make you mad!

20:18.780 --> 20:22.240
Yeah! So we showed off like clang-clang!

20:23.280 --> 20:26.160
I looked depressed?

20:26.160 --> 20:27.830
Huh? Yeah...

20:27.830 --> 20:29.700
You looked really down lately...

20:29.700 --> 20:30.790
Right.

20:30.790 --> 20:33.250
You haven't exactly been a ray of sunshine lately, Alice.

20:34.370 --> 20:35.540
Ace!

20:36.000 --> 20:37.540
What are you doing?

20:37.540 --> 20:39.050
What does it look like?

20:39.050 --> 20:42.590
I don't know. Why are you on the chandelier?

20:43.130 --> 20:45.510
It's just how it looks! I'm slacking off!

20:45.510 --> 20:50.220
A knave shouldn't have to stand guard at a ball.

20:51.600 --> 20:54.480
Ace! What are you doing?!

20:56.310 --> 20:58.690
Do not go near Alice!

20:58.690 --> 20:59.770
What?

20:59.770 --> 21:02.110
You can join us, Peter.

21:02.110 --> 21:05.490
I am a rabbit who's diligent in his duties, unlike you.

21:05.490 --> 21:08.450
Oh, Alice, I love you so.

21:08.450 --> 21:10.330
Please dance with me.

21:11.910 --> 21:14.210
If you're so diligent, then get to work.

21:14.960 --> 21:17.210
You've got work, too.

21:20.500 --> 21:21.420
What?

21:23.090 --> 21:25.880
It's finally the ball, so let's dance.

21:25.880 --> 21:28.090
What are you doing?! Put me down!

21:28.720 --> 21:31.600
Oh, Alice. Do you have a death wish?

21:31.600 --> 21:33.390
If you fall, you'll die.

21:38.270 --> 21:40.400
What gives, Peter?

21:40.400 --> 21:41.940
That's dangerous!

21:41.940 --> 21:43.740
<i>You're</i> dangerous!

21:43.740 --> 21:45.530
Release Alice.

21:45.530 --> 21:49.160
First Alice, now you too, Peter...

21:49.160 --> 21:50.780
You want me to let go?

21:50.780 --> 21:53.160
Don't let go! You can't let go!

21:53.750 --> 21:55.620
You're pretty fierce!

21:55.620 --> 21:59.710
See that, Peter? Alice said so herself!

22:05.840 --> 22:10.470
Aw, geez, Peter. The ball's only just begun!

22:19.900 --> 22:21.310
Jump, Alice!

22:23.360 --> 22:24.440
Again!

22:26.070 --> 22:27.240
Once more!

22:27.240 --> 22:28.360
N-No, wait!

22:38.420 --> 22:39.620
Hold on!

22:49.340 --> 22:50.180
Alice!

22:51.470 --> 22:53.600
Just my luck!

22:56.600 --> 22:58.850
Will she be all right?

22:58.850 --> 23:00.190
Is she okay?

23:01.480 --> 23:03.900
I'm going to fall!

23:08.450 --> 23:09.780
Ace, get down here!

23:09.780 --> 23:11.360
Er...

23:11.360 --> 23:13.410
Julius, are you mad?

23:13.410 --> 23:14.780
A little.

23:14.780 --> 23:18.330
I'm more than a <i>little</i> mad at you!

23:18.330 --> 23:21.250
Get down here, you bastard!

23:26.050 --> 23:29.670
Honestly, they're all so impossible.

23:29.670 --> 23:32.930
I agree, but you're one to talk.

23:36.640 --> 23:38.890
I lost the vial...

23:38.890 --> 23:39.770
Hm?

23:40.100 --> 23:44.690
That was my key to go home, yet I lost it somewhere.

23:45.020 --> 23:47.030
Is... that right?

23:47.030 --> 23:48.900
Oh, you're not happy?

23:48.900 --> 23:51.910
I thought you'd be glad I can't go home now.

23:54.120 --> 23:57.120
I'm very glad that you came here,

23:57.490 --> 24:02.040
but that vial... isn't something that's easily lost.

24:02.040 --> 24:05.460
Even though you say that, I lost it!

24:05.460 --> 24:07.590
You simply cannot see it.

24:07.590 --> 24:11.720
No matter how I wish it were so, it will not leave you

24:11.720 --> 24:13.550
because it is your...

24:17.100 --> 24:18.970
It turned into evening.

24:20.230 --> 24:22.520
What an arbitrary world this is.

24:24.350 --> 24:26.230
Anyway, I still have to go back.

24:26.690 --> 24:28.980
Do you want to go home, Alice?

24:29.780 --> 24:32.110
The ball is already over.

24:32.110 --> 24:35.620
The Hatter group may not look it, but they're easily worried.

24:35.620 --> 24:37.370
I need go back with them.

24:37.370 --> 24:40.580
They won't leave the castle until they find me.

24:40.580 --> 24:42.620
That's not what I mean.

24:43.120 --> 24:44.870
Do you want to go home?

24:44.870 --> 24:46.420
Back to your world.

24:48.880 --> 24:50.170
Yes.

24:50.170 --> 24:54.470
But it's evening, so I'll have to wait until the right time to go.

24:54.470 --> 24:57.300
Though I'm starting to think that being here isn't so bad.

25:04.690 --> 25:06.400
Please don't go home.

25:06.400 --> 25:08.650
You want me to stay at the castle?

25:09.320 --> 25:12.070
I wish you would do that, but...

25:12.530 --> 25:16.820
if it would restrain you, you do not have to.

25:16.820 --> 25:19.080
You wouldn't be restraining me.

25:19.080 --> 25:22.330
Even then, we don't have to meet.

25:22.660 --> 25:25.580
You don't even have to see me.

25:26.040 --> 25:29.090
I don't care where you live.

25:29.090 --> 25:32.300
If I can't see you, I'll live with my heartache.

25:32.630 --> 25:35.340
So as long as you don't go home...

25:37.180 --> 25:39.180
The castle is like a dream,

25:39.180 --> 25:41.640
but my home is somewhere else.

25:42.020 --> 25:48.860
If I get attached here, then I might be forced to stay in this world.

26:24.430 --> 26:26.770
Why aren'tcha guys eatin'?

26:28.060 --> 26:30.020
Man, it's a disaster!

26:30.020 --> 26:31.690
A huge disaster!

26:31.690 --> 26:34.280
It's evening tea time, yet the boss isn't here.

26:34.280 --> 26:36.320
So Onee-san isn't herself.

26:36.320 --> 26:37.780
Wh-What?

26:38.110 --> 26:39.280
Nothing.

26:39.280 --> 26:41.950
We told you that the boss has been busy lately.

26:41.950 --> 26:45.370
Ah! Is that why you're so glum?

26:45.370 --> 26:47.580
Th-That's stupid!

26:47.580 --> 26:50.210
Why would I be sad that Blood isn't here?!

27:03.510 --> 27:04.310
Say...

27:04.970 --> 27:08.230
I lost my vial, but can I still go home?

27:08.980 --> 27:10.690
I'm not the one to ask.

27:10.690 --> 27:14.070
Do you think... I should go home?

27:23.490 --> 27:25.540
You decide for yourself.

27:25.540 --> 27:27.500
What do you think?

27:27.500 --> 27:28.870
I think...

27:31.620 --> 27:34.000
you aren't meant to be here.

27:34.000 --> 27:35.670
What do you mean?

27:35.670 --> 27:39.170
No matter what they say, you'll never belong.

27:39.170 --> 27:40.840
Not while you have a heart.

27:40.840 --> 27:43.930
Because I'm... an outsider?

27:43.930 --> 27:46.600
Yes. You are an outsider.

27:46.600 --> 27:49.600
As long as you're here, you won't fit in.

27:50.100 --> 27:51.520
And that is that.

27:51.940 --> 27:55.150
Alice, you shouldn't be here.

27:55.570 --> 27:59.030
That is what I think, whether or not you have the vial.

27:59.030 --> 28:00.860
I will never...

28:01.280 --> 28:03.990
However, this is just my opinion.

28:03.990 --> 28:09.580
Where is your home? What path will you choose? You need to decide.

28:11.750 --> 28:16.000
Even if you don't, clocks will tick and life will go on.

28:16.460 --> 28:18.420
That must bring about your decision.

28:39.360 --> 28:41.610
You! You are irritating!

28:41.610 --> 28:44.200
How irritating! How very irritating!

28:44.200 --> 28:46.200
Your head must roll!

28:46.200 --> 28:48.120
But who will execute me?

28:48.490 --> 28:50.370
You're so fussy...

28:50.370 --> 28:52.870
Yes, you're as bad as the Hatter!

28:52.870 --> 28:55.630
How dare that lout make us wait!

28:55.630 --> 28:57.790
Oh, he's so irritating!

28:58.670 --> 29:00.050
Settle down.

29:00.380 --> 29:05.130
Hysterics will only make him irritated when he gets here, too.

29:05.130 --> 29:06.220
What?

29:06.220 --> 29:09.430
If he doesn't listen, then <i>your</i> head will roll!

29:16.190 --> 29:18.150
Huh? A substitute?

29:18.520 --> 29:20.940
Only leaders are allowed here.

29:20.940 --> 29:23.780
Nah, I'm just the messenger.

29:24.150 --> 29:26.320
Blood can't make it.

29:26.320 --> 29:27.530
What was that?!

29:27.530 --> 29:29.370
<i>He</i> made us wait here!

29:29.370 --> 29:32.870
Is there a reason for his absence?

29:32.870 --> 29:35.920
Something important came up.

29:35.920 --> 29:38.000
That is no reason.

29:38.000 --> 29:41.920
There's always something up with your lot.

29:41.920 --> 29:45.260
It's not for any stupid reason.

29:45.260 --> 29:50.760
Anyway, Blood is busy, so that's why he can't come.

29:50.760 --> 29:56.270
He gets in shady places, and you just fumble around with clocks.

29:56.770 --> 29:58.650
For that, I'm glad.

29:58.650 --> 30:02.780
I would never want to be grouped in with the likes of <i>you</i>.

30:15.790 --> 30:21.340
Your guard-dogs seem to think of my men as toys.

30:21.340 --> 30:23.590
What of it?

30:23.590 --> 30:27.260
It wouldn't be fun for them if they didn't have toys.

30:27.260 --> 30:28.470
Is that so?

30:28.470 --> 30:30.930
Then if they weren't toying with them...

30:31.390 --> 30:34.640
You're admitting that your men were being toyed with?

30:34.640 --> 30:35.560
You bastard!

30:35.560 --> 30:36.680
No,

30:36.680 --> 30:38.140
I am not.

30:47.280 --> 30:52.450
I do not need subordinates that will be treated like toys.

30:55.370 --> 30:57.460
So remember this:

30:57.460 --> 31:00.290
One day, it will be your turn to be toyed with.

31:00.790 --> 31:02.460
I look forward to it.

31:16.850 --> 31:19.140
I'll go on by myself from here.

31:19.140 --> 31:20.140
What?

31:20.140 --> 31:22.810
But we're still in enemy territory.

31:23.150 --> 31:24.690
It's dangerous, Boss.

31:24.690 --> 31:27.110
Who do you think I am?

31:27.110 --> 31:28.530
I beg your pardon!

31:44.040 --> 31:45.170
Hiya!

31:45.170 --> 31:48.630
Well, look who it is. One of the Jokers.

31:48.630 --> 31:51.380
Are you disappointed that it's only one?

31:51.380 --> 31:55.390
Not at all. In fact, I didn't want to see either of you.

31:55.390 --> 31:58.140
You're just the easier one to deal with.

31:59.350 --> 32:01.310
That's what you think!

32:03.560 --> 32:06.820
You've broken the rules!

32:06.820 --> 32:09.030
Act mature and take your punishment!

32:09.570 --> 32:11.360
What a thing to say!

32:11.360 --> 32:14.280
You shouldn't stick your nose in the Mafia's affairs.

32:14.280 --> 32:15.700
Are you kidding?

32:15.700 --> 32:18.370
Who'd be interested in what the Mafia does?

32:18.370 --> 32:20.250
<i>You're</i> the rule breaker!

32:21.540 --> 32:23.620
I was not kidding in the least.

32:23.620 --> 32:28.630
You say I've done wrong, but I've not the slightest idea what you mean.

32:32.050 --> 32:34.050
Trying to run away?

32:34.050 --> 32:35.600
Come play with me!

32:35.600 --> 32:39.600
Sorry, but I'm not interested in playing with men.

32:49.570 --> 32:50.650
Blood...

32:51.030 --> 32:54.490
What's wrong, Miss? To come here...

32:54.490 --> 32:58.160
Actually, I was looking for you.

32:58.160 --> 33:00.660
I thought you'd be in the mansion.

33:01.250 --> 33:04.170
Should I not have come here?

33:04.170 --> 33:05.630
Not quite.

33:05.630 --> 33:09.340
Well, you won't find much in the basement other than darkness where you could hurt yourself.

33:09.670 --> 33:11.800
You shouldn't go on.

33:12.300 --> 33:13.800
I'm sorry.

33:13.800 --> 33:14.880
Don't be.

33:14.880 --> 33:20.140
But usually you would wait enduringly for my return.

33:20.140 --> 33:21.720
What was it you needed?

33:22.020 --> 33:24.890
It's like you're scolding me.

33:24.890 --> 33:27.230
It makes you seem so mean.

33:27.230 --> 33:30.610
Would you rather I be gracious and pure?

33:30.610 --> 33:32.610
No, that's all right.

33:32.610 --> 33:34.650
I don't think I'd like that.

33:34.650 --> 33:36.110
You wouldn't be the same.

33:36.110 --> 33:38.410
You're different today.

33:38.410 --> 33:41.120
If you have something to say, then do so.

33:41.660 --> 33:43.870
Wasn't that why you were looking for me?

33:43.870 --> 33:45.040
Well...

33:45.040 --> 33:49.710
I don't want to be rude, but... can I stay here a little while longer?

33:50.710 --> 33:52.050
As long as you'd like.

33:52.050 --> 33:55.420
But... my reason for staying has changed.

33:55.420 --> 33:59.970
To be honest, I didn't think I'd stay here for so long.

33:59.970 --> 34:01.010
Though—

34:01.600 --> 34:04.100
That's enough, Miss.

34:04.100 --> 34:06.190
Stay here as long as you'd like.

34:07.060 --> 34:08.520
Thank you.

34:08.520 --> 34:10.360
No need to thank me.

34:10.360 --> 34:13.190
A-Anyway, what was that room?

34:13.190 --> 34:17.490
I've never been in the basement, so I was kind of curious.

34:17.490 --> 34:18.780
Ah...

34:24.450 --> 34:26.160
It's a wine cellar.

34:27.000 --> 34:28.920
You have a great collection!

34:28.920 --> 34:31.840
Yes. Do you want to try some, too?

34:31.840 --> 34:33.380
Too?

34:35.300 --> 34:39.430
You mean... you were slacking off from work to drink?

34:39.430 --> 34:41.390
You smell like wine!

34:42.390 --> 34:45.520
Tasting exquisite drinks is part of my job.

34:54.690 --> 34:56.240
Execute him!

34:56.240 --> 34:58.200
Chop off his head and be done with it!

34:59.070 --> 35:01.070
H-Have mercy!

35:01.070 --> 35:04.660
Are we not merciful by sparing you torture?

35:04.660 --> 35:08.620
Be thankful. We are not in a foul mood.

35:08.620 --> 35:10.880
Praise our benevolent Majesty!

35:13.000 --> 35:15.210
Bring in the next offender.

35:19.180 --> 35:21.180
Off with his head.

35:21.550 --> 35:25.810
Your Majesty, I haven't even told you his offense.

35:25.810 --> 35:26.850
You haven't?

35:26.850 --> 35:30.270
Then don't do that. Just hang him.

35:30.270 --> 35:34.020
Yes, but we haven't even charged him with anything yet!

35:34.570 --> 35:36.690
Are you sassing your queen?

35:36.690 --> 35:39.650
What do you think his sentence should be?

35:41.700 --> 35:44.030
Then, the next offender.

35:44.580 --> 35:46.370
Anything but that!

35:46.370 --> 35:48.660
The next offender is a castle maid.

35:52.630 --> 35:54.250
Her offense is...

35:54.250 --> 35:57.920
putting two lumps of sugar in the queen's tea.

35:57.920 --> 36:00.010
Hey, what are you doing?

36:00.010 --> 36:01.590
Oh, Alice!

36:01.590 --> 36:06.100
The queen only likes one lump of sugar in her tea.

36:06.470 --> 36:07.770
And?

36:07.770 --> 36:12.100
That maid mistakenly put two lumps in her tea.

36:12.100 --> 36:13.400
So?

36:13.400 --> 36:16.570
So we are holding her trial!

36:16.570 --> 36:19.070
Do you know what a trial <i>is</i>?

36:19.070 --> 36:21.030
Of course I know.

36:21.030 --> 36:25.530
I read the list of offenses and the queen passes judgment.

36:25.530 --> 36:29.580
How is that a trial? You don't even have a jury!

36:29.580 --> 36:36.210
We used to have one, but they passed a sentence that the queen didn't like, and she had them executed.

36:36.210 --> 36:37.210
All of them.

36:38.300 --> 36:40.170
Yes, all of them.

36:40.170 --> 36:42.420
They annoyed her.

36:42.420 --> 36:47.510
Putting two lumps of sugar is foolish, but at least she's giving her a trial.

36:47.930 --> 36:51.140
Anyway, the trials go by much faster now.

36:51.140 --> 36:55.730
Say, Alice, when I'm done, do you want to go somewhere?

36:55.730 --> 36:57.190
Go somewhere?

36:57.190 --> 36:59.650
There are only six more trials to go.

36:59.650 --> 37:02.700
Six trials will take a long time.

37:02.700 --> 37:03.950
I'll make them quick!

37:03.950 --> 37:08.240
A trial isn't something that's meant to be over quickly...

37:08.240 --> 37:09.740
Off with her head!

37:09.740 --> 37:10.700
See?

37:10.700 --> 37:12.040
Vivaldi!

37:12.750 --> 37:14.250
What is it, Alice?

37:14.250 --> 37:18.710
We are busy thinking of a suitable punishment. Come back later.

37:18.710 --> 37:21.380
You can't give everyone the same sentence.

37:21.380 --> 37:22.720
We do not.

37:22.720 --> 37:25.260
Sometimes we change the method of execution.

37:26.590 --> 37:28.010
Are you tired?

37:28.010 --> 37:29.970
We are simply bored.

37:32.520 --> 37:33.480
It's night...

37:34.520 --> 37:38.400
Goodness... Even the daytime is bored.

37:40.900 --> 37:43.490
Our work for today is done.

37:43.490 --> 37:44.700
Your Majesty!

37:44.700 --> 37:48.950
We're holding trials for those who have incurred your anger.

37:48.950 --> 37:51.740
There's a few more to go, so please bear with it!

37:52.870 --> 37:55.210
How many are left?

37:55.210 --> 37:57.500
There are six left.

38:00.920 --> 38:02.420
Let's see...

38:02.420 --> 38:07.430
Next is a cook who prepared thoroughly done ham and eggs for the queen's breakfast.

38:07.970 --> 38:09.600
Say, Vivaldi!

38:10.600 --> 38:13.140
If you're tired, you should sleep!

38:13.140 --> 38:15.640
Lack of sleep affects your beauty!

38:15.640 --> 38:18.310
You should sleep right away!

38:18.310 --> 38:19.360
Right? Right?

38:19.980 --> 38:21.900
It appears so.

38:21.900 --> 38:23.530
Then we will do that.

38:23.530 --> 38:26.570
But we're in a trial. What shall we do?

38:26.570 --> 38:28.200
Oh, that's right.

38:28.200 --> 38:30.910
Execute the rest as you see fit.

38:30.910 --> 38:31.990
Vivaldi!

38:31.990 --> 38:33.620
What was that?

38:33.620 --> 38:35.290
Do not raise your voice!

38:35.290 --> 38:37.710
If you disagree with us, then the out—

38:37.710 --> 38:40.000
I want to take over the trials!

38:40.000 --> 38:41.040
What?

38:41.040 --> 38:43.420
I'll judge for you!

38:43.420 --> 38:45.710
So you can sleep without worry!

38:45.710 --> 38:48.680
Can we not just execute them all?

38:48.680 --> 38:49.680
You can't!

38:49.680 --> 38:53.850
U-Um, I'm not saying you can't, just that you probably shouldn't.

38:53.850 --> 38:57.230
Also, I've always wanted to try being a judge!

38:57.230 --> 38:59.770
So, please, will you let me do it?

39:02.190 --> 39:03.150
No?

39:03.150 --> 39:06.820
We didn't think you would want
to do such a boring job.

39:06.820 --> 39:09.990
How curious your interests are.

39:16.000 --> 39:17.750
What's with this sceptre?

39:17.750 --> 39:19.710
It grants you our power.

39:20.750 --> 39:22.500
Oh, Vivaldi!

39:22.500 --> 39:25.920
Next time you have a trial, you have to invite me, okay?

39:26.590 --> 39:27.970
Do what you wish.

39:27.970 --> 39:32.180
If you still want to be the judge then, we will let you.

39:37.850 --> 39:39.690
Peter, you heard that?

39:39.690 --> 39:43.230
Yes, very well! My ears are excellent!

39:43.230 --> 39:47.990
But I didn't know you liked judging others so much!

39:47.990 --> 39:50.780
I wish you would have told me sooner.

39:50.780 --> 39:54.280
Now I can add more people to the list!

39:54.280 --> 39:56.620
Don't be stupid!

39:56.620 --> 39:58.330
You need your rest, too.

39:58.330 --> 40:01.620
However, we need to get through the ones you have.

40:01.620 --> 40:02.500
What?

40:02.500 --> 40:05.670
But we've already sentenced them.

40:05.670 --> 40:08.590
Hm... beheading, beheading, hanging...

40:08.590 --> 40:13.010
I don't even have to read them. Just death, death, death!

40:13.590 --> 40:15.390
Do you think otherwise?

40:15.390 --> 40:19.270
I heard what they did, but all those charges are stupid!

40:19.270 --> 40:21.770
But I don't want to retry them...

40:21.770 --> 40:26.270
In any case, it's much more fun to go out and play with me!

40:26.270 --> 40:28.780
Forget about what happens to them!

40:28.780 --> 40:31.360
There will be plenty of people for you to judge next time!

40:31.360 --> 40:34.870
Let's hurry and end work today!

40:34.870 --> 40:38.080
You're so ridiculous for a rabbit!

40:38.080 --> 40:40.080
<i>I'm</i> the judge!

40:40.080 --> 40:42.370
So you have to listen to <i>me</i>!

40:43.040 --> 40:46.250
If you don't, I'll have your head chopped off!

40:48.380 --> 40:49.880
That's wonderful!

40:49.880 --> 40:51.470
You sound like a tyrant!

40:51.470 --> 40:54.300
Huh? You're the last one to talk!

40:54.300 --> 40:56.180
If anyone, <i>you</i> are the tyrant!

40:56.180 --> 40:57.720
Me, a tyrant?!

40:57.720 --> 41:00.890
I am no more than the castle's prime minister.

41:00.890 --> 41:02.230
I just follow orders.

41:03.140 --> 41:05.650
You're going to change their sentences, aren't you?

41:05.650 --> 41:09.780
Then tell me, how do you rule them, Your Honor?

41:09.780 --> 41:11.110
Innocent.

41:11.110 --> 41:13.860
Actually, they must be punished!

41:13.860 --> 41:18.330
The punishment for the maid whom put
two lumps of sugar in the queen's tea is...

41:18.330 --> 41:20.540
to make sure she doesn't do it again!

41:21.330 --> 41:23.620
Her tea should have one lump.

41:23.620 --> 41:28.000
To ensure this, the maid must drink tea
as the queen likes it so as to not get confused.

41:29.840 --> 41:34.300
For the cook who prepared thoroughly done
ham and eggs for the queen's breakfast...

41:34.300 --> 41:36.090
Huh? Me, too?

41:36.090 --> 41:37.090
Of course.

41:37.090 --> 41:40.720
From now on, remember to prepare
her ham and eggs only half-cooked.

41:40.720 --> 41:42.390
Don't overcook it.

41:42.390 --> 41:45.270
That's like they're innocent.

41:45.270 --> 41:47.480
Goodness, no! They are being punished.

41:47.480 --> 41:50.900
Not being able to drink tea as you like it...

41:50.900 --> 41:52.230
is just torture!

41:53.990 --> 41:58.320
And not being able to cook ham
and eggs as you like it, too... right?

41:58.320 --> 42:00.200
Isn't that torture?

42:00.200 --> 42:01.990
Do you think so?

42:01.990 --> 42:07.170
I'm not that picky about my sugar
or how my ham and eggs are cooked...

42:07.170 --> 42:11.920
Vivaldi would think I gave them a sentence worse than death.

42:11.920 --> 42:14.340
So it's torture, isn't it?

42:14.340 --> 42:18.430
I will give the other offenders
an equally cruel punishment.

42:22.140 --> 42:25.520
You're too nice to the faceless people.

42:26.520 --> 42:28.600
And too nice to others...

42:28.600 --> 42:31.060
but you're so cold with me.

42:33.280 --> 42:35.240
Something wrong, Peter?

42:35.240 --> 42:36.650
No, not at all!

42:38.570 --> 42:41.280
Speaking of which, what brought you here?

42:41.280 --> 42:45.830
Ever since I lost my vial,
I haven't been able to keep myself calm.

42:45.830 --> 42:48.420
I thought some change of pace might help me.

42:48.790 --> 42:50.000
I see.

42:50.960 --> 42:54.050
You're right. It might help.

42:54.050 --> 42:55.960
I hope so.

42:55.960 --> 42:58.970
Maybe I only say that due to my feelings.

42:59.470 --> 43:03.760
But if I don't, then I'll never find my vial.

43:03.760 --> 43:08.140
Yes. Like you, I only say that due to my heart.

43:08.140 --> 43:11.900
In this world, time goes back and forth,

43:11.900 --> 43:14.690
so the vial may also come and go.

43:15.070 --> 43:17.650
It may also come back to you.

43:17.650 --> 43:19.950
Because this is Wonderland?

43:22.620 --> 43:23.830
Precisely.

43:23.830 --> 43:25.950
Because this is the Country of Hearts!

44:36.440 --> 44:39.820
Innocent. Actually, they must be punished!

45:02.550 --> 45:03.590
What now?

45:03.970 --> 45:06.720
You, too? You still get lost?

45:06.720 --> 45:08.510
We are not lost.

45:08.510 --> 45:10.180
We are simply mad.

45:10.180 --> 45:12.270
We have bared our annoyance long enough.

45:12.270 --> 45:16.190
If you have time to dawdle with that junk, fix our clock!

45:16.190 --> 45:19.520
Your clock isn't broken, so there is nothing to fix.

45:20.730 --> 45:22.070
Useless fool.

45:43.920 --> 45:46.390
And then, see those barons...

45:46.390 --> 45:48.680
Actually, one of my servants...

46:01.570 --> 46:02.820
You're late.

46:02.820 --> 46:04.150
Were we?

46:04.150 --> 46:08.450
So says the man who is too self-important to apologize for missing our appointment.

46:08.450 --> 46:10.160
Were you going to return the favor?

46:10.160 --> 46:12.410
Does it look like it?

46:12.410 --> 46:16.710
We never thought you would host a garden party for the upper class.

46:16.710 --> 46:18.960
I suppose I understand.

46:18.960 --> 46:21.210
I hate the nobility.

46:21.710 --> 46:24.170
Do you hate how carefree they look?

46:24.170 --> 46:27.090
I don't have any ill thoughts toward them,

46:27.090 --> 46:28.510
but I cannot stand them.

46:29.510 --> 46:33.390
So you say, yet you wish to be more like them.

46:33.390 --> 46:33.970
Sister—

46:33.970 --> 46:35.680
If you wish to go somewhere,

46:35.680 --> 46:37.850
you will not refuse if given the chance,

46:37.850 --> 46:38.900
no?

46:39.400 --> 46:41.360
What hole did you crawl out of?

46:41.360 --> 46:42.730
You filthy worm...

46:42.730 --> 46:44.150
No, you caterpillar!

46:44.900 --> 46:47.240
But I can go anywhere I please.

46:47.240 --> 46:49.240
I'm a nightmare after all.

46:49.240 --> 46:50.530
Not to mention,

46:50.530 --> 46:54.080
it's especially easy to enter a rulebreaker's territory.

46:54.080 --> 46:56.750
Did you come here to lecture us?

46:56.750 --> 46:59.500
Not to lecture, but to warn you.

46:59.500 --> 47:02.040
There are penalties for breaking the rules.

47:02.880 --> 47:04.920
So what exactly are you implying?

47:06.840 --> 47:11.090
The two of you... don't have any guilt-ridden dreams of what you've done?

47:11.970 --> 47:16.770
We are not children, so our dreams should not have any bearing on us.

47:31.450 --> 47:33.240
That was some obtrusion.

47:33.240 --> 47:35.700
Only because I chose that place.

47:35.700 --> 47:38.870
Nothing about it was pleasant except for the tea.

47:38.870 --> 47:40.330
Don't say that.

47:40.790 --> 47:42.080
Come with us.

48:04.150 --> 48:05.480
It is time.

48:07.610 --> 48:08.820
I have to go.

48:11.070 --> 48:13.280
I'm young, but these are the rules.

48:13.280 --> 48:15.830
This is the duty of a noble's daughter.

48:18.330 --> 48:21.410
We can't be together, but we'll be in each other's hearts.

48:24.580 --> 48:26.460
In our hearts?

48:26.460 --> 48:27.460
Yes.

48:27.460 --> 48:29.090
In our hearts.

48:33.720 --> 48:35.100
This is the end.

48:35.100 --> 48:37.220
You must forget us.

48:41.810 --> 48:44.310
No! I don't want to forget!

48:48.150 --> 48:52.150
I wish time would have stopped when we didn't have to forget.

48:54.110 --> 48:57.740
What a very boring, frustrating likeness.

48:57.740 --> 49:00.000
Yes, very.

49:20.720 --> 49:22.890
We lost the key,

49:22.890 --> 49:25.020
so we cannot get out.

49:25.020 --> 49:26.480
Yes, you can.

49:26.480 --> 49:28.400
The key is right here.

49:36.240 --> 49:38.530
I lost my vial.

49:59.390 --> 50:03.220
Well, well, look who it is! Hänsel and Gretel!

50:03.980 --> 50:06.560
So you finally came to visit, huh?

50:07.150 --> 50:09.310
Do not jest, Clown.

50:09.310 --> 50:11.230
Clowns are meant to jest,

50:11.230 --> 50:13.280
so I act like a jester.

50:13.280 --> 50:16.950
But at the moment, I am not jesting, Hänsel and Gretel.

50:17.320 --> 50:20.490
The siblings who wandered into the gingerbread house.

50:20.490 --> 50:22.490
You <i>must</i> be kidding.

50:22.490 --> 50:27.250
We are nothing like big brother and little sister, but big sister and little brother.

50:27.250 --> 50:31.880
Also, this is no gingerbread house, but rather a rubbish bin.

50:35.920 --> 50:37.590
But isn't it the same?

50:37.590 --> 50:40.720
The both of you are wandering astray.

50:43.680 --> 50:47.230
Do you pity her? The lost little girl?

50:57.360 --> 51:00.620
No, you don't pity her.
You sympathize with her, right?

51:00.620 --> 51:02.240
You still kid.

51:02.240 --> 51:03.330
We are...

51:04.240 --> 51:06.710
already free.

51:07.540 --> 51:12.500
You've escaped from the prison, but you'll always be a prisoner in this world.

51:12.500 --> 51:14.800
But I'm sure you knew that.

51:14.800 --> 51:16.880
This world is meaningless.

51:17.550 --> 51:19.930
Meaningless, huh?

51:20.430 --> 51:23.220
Then tell me, Hatter—Blood Dupre,

51:23.600 --> 51:26.600
was it meaningless to help your sister?

51:26.600 --> 51:31.350
And you're not responsible for sheltering that outsider your sister is obsessed with?

51:31.350 --> 51:33.820
Exactly. It's meaningless.

51:34.150 --> 51:36.860
I'm not sheltering her, either.

51:36.860 --> 51:40.780
Really? Then everything is meaningless to you, isn't it—

51:43.830 --> 51:47.160
The things you say are even more meaningless.

51:47.160 --> 51:49.250
An absolute waste of time.

51:54.420 --> 51:55.550
Yes!

51:55.550 --> 51:58.340
Yes, nothing matters!

51:58.840 --> 52:01.260
Not even how many times you kill me!

52:03.260 --> 52:06.060
We no longer fear prison.

52:06.060 --> 52:08.770
We may hate it, but do not fear it.

52:30.660 --> 52:33.420
Good grief, he got himself killed again.

52:33.420 --> 52:35.540
Worthless Joker.

52:35.540 --> 52:38.840
Won't a new Joker be made soon, though?

52:38.840 --> 52:41.340
That's why he's worthless!

52:43.550 --> 52:45.930
Hänsel and Gretel?

52:46.430 --> 52:53.350
Well, those two that tried to kill the witch are dangerous. Not to be taken lightly.

52:53.770 --> 52:57.270
Even Alice can't capture them.

52:57.270 --> 52:58.900
What should we do, Ace?

52:59.940 --> 53:02.400
It's all the same to me.

53:02.400 --> 53:05.620
If we can't catch them, we'll kill them.

53:07.580 --> 53:09.330
Ugh, he's so aggravating!

53:09.330 --> 53:10.660
He irritates me!

53:10.660 --> 53:13.870
Calm down, Sister. He won't come for us.

53:27.390 --> 53:30.600
So, I'm really proud of you, Nee-san.

53:30.600 --> 53:33.100
Oh, why thank you.

53:33.100 --> 53:36.150
Then I must be honest, Alice.

53:36.150 --> 53:38.570
I'm proud of you, too!

54:18.100 --> 54:21.150
May we ask you something, Blood?

54:21.150 --> 54:24.070
Do you sympathize with her?

54:24.490 --> 54:27.320
I also have something to ask, Sister.

54:27.740 --> 54:30.370
Does it seem like I do things out of pity?

54:34.620 --> 54:41.210
For my benefit, or in order to kill some time, maybe, but doing something for someone else? Never.

54:41.840 --> 54:43.840
You ask me spectacular things.

54:44.420 --> 54:45.720
Of course.

54:45.720 --> 54:49.260
That is why we trust you.

54:50.760 --> 54:52.600
That's why?

54:52.600 --> 54:55.140
I'm flattered, but why is that?

54:55.140 --> 54:58.730
Because you are wicked,
but do not pretend to be good.

55:07.070 --> 55:09.200
You are a heartless man.

55:09.200 --> 55:12.620
Where is the boy I kept in my heart for so long?

55:12.620 --> 55:15.120
Time is a harsh mistress.

55:15.120 --> 55:18.330
She does not relent for anyone here.

55:21.750 --> 55:23.130
That's right.

55:23.130 --> 55:25.460
We don't need to keep others in our hearts.

55:25.460 --> 55:30.180
Hearts are meaningless—all of us act according to our clocks.

55:30.180 --> 55:32.470
Yes, all of us.

55:32.470 --> 55:34.430
Acting meaninglessly...

56:03.670 --> 56:05.880
It still hasn't come back.

56:06.630 --> 56:09.590
I guess I shouldn't be surprised.

56:09.590 --> 56:12.680
It won't just come and go like that.

56:22.150 --> 56:24.400
Are you having fun, Alice?

56:24.400 --> 56:27.570
Of course I am... <i>not</i>!

56:28.230 --> 56:31.150
You're not having fun at an amusement park?!

56:31.150 --> 56:32.820
Don't you like rollercoasters?

56:32.820 --> 56:37.620
I do! But I would like them more without you playing—!

56:37.620 --> 56:38.830
Isn't it harmonious?

56:38.830 --> 56:40.000
It's a cacophony!

56:40.000 --> 56:43.170
It's so bad, I feel like the coaster's gonna break down!

56:43.540 --> 56:45.920
Sometimes it <i>does</i> break down!

56:45.920 --> 56:47.170
W-What?

56:47.170 --> 56:49.800
This coaster goes off the track every so often.

56:49.800 --> 56:51.300
So—meti—mes!

56:52.220 --> 56:53.970
Isn't it exciting?

56:55.390 --> 56:58.350
Let me off—!

57:01.640 --> 57:03.730
Alice, are you okay?

57:03.730 --> 57:04.810
I feel sick...

57:04.810 --> 57:07.150
Do you? That's too bad.

57:07.150 --> 57:09.320
I'll play something to make you feel better...

57:09.320 --> 57:10.740
H-H-Hold on!

57:10.740 --> 57:13.450
Time out! Let's take a break!

57:13.450 --> 57:15.620
Yeah, a song will ease your stomach.

57:15.620 --> 57:18.830
Give it a rest, Old Man! Are you trying to kill us?

57:19.160 --> 57:22.540
Let's go buy something cold to eat, Boris!

57:23.160 --> 57:24.210
Thank you.

57:26.630 --> 57:28.420
Are you worried about something?

57:28.420 --> 57:30.590
Huh? Why would I be?

57:30.590 --> 57:33.510
You look like you need a change of pace.

57:33.510 --> 57:36.260
Do I really look like it?

57:42.850 --> 57:45.600
I shouldn't act like this.

57:45.600 --> 57:48.230
Sorry I spent the day like this.

57:48.230 --> 57:49.690
That's all right.

57:49.690 --> 57:52.570
Even though I finally came to the amusement park...

57:52.570 --> 57:55.530
I said it's fine. You're special.

57:56.450 --> 57:58.870
The only people here are faceless.

57:59.330 --> 58:01.410
You're the one exception.

58:01.740 --> 58:03.580
Don't say that...

58:04.370 --> 58:06.210
I'm glad, but it makes me feel lonely—

58:09.130 --> 58:10.250
Boris?

58:10.250 --> 58:12.880
Would you like some? It's delicious!

58:12.880 --> 58:15.840
This is the attraction that just opened up!

58:16.590 --> 58:18.930
Did you enjoy the ride?

58:18.930 --> 58:20.430
Yeah, but it was kind of...

58:20.430 --> 58:22.390
Let's go see the parade.

58:22.390 --> 58:24.890
Oh, let's go to the next ride.

58:27.270 --> 58:28.730
Miss...

58:29.190 --> 58:31.110
would you like a balloon?

58:31.110 --> 58:32.650
It's you...

58:32.650 --> 58:34.610
You can have it.

58:34.610 --> 58:38.280
In return, will you visit our new attraction?

58:57.090 --> 58:58.430
What should I do?

58:58.800 --> 59:00.720
I can't find the exit.

59:01.180 --> 59:03.720
I can't find the entrance, either.

59:03.720 --> 59:05.520
I've gotten really lost.

59:08.600 --> 59:10.980
Isn't it awful to be lost?

59:14.780 --> 59:16.190
This is a dream.

59:16.530 --> 59:19.110
I'm just still in a dream.

59:19.110 --> 59:22.070
No, this whole world is a dream.

59:22.070 --> 59:24.740
If so, then it must be a bad dream.

59:33.460 --> 59:36.210
A maze of unending worry.

59:51.480 --> 59:52.860
Over here!

59:54.570 --> 59:55.900
Peter?!

59:58.110 --> 59:59.950
Over here, Alice!

1:00:05.490 --> 1:00:06.830
Over here!

1:00:13.670 --> 1:00:14.960
This door...

1:00:15.590 --> 1:00:17.710
This is it, Alice.

1:00:17.710 --> 1:00:20.170
You will be happy here.

1:00:20.880 --> 1:00:22.890
I'll be happy there?

1:00:22.890 --> 1:00:25.550
Yes, just come with me

1:00:25.550 --> 1:00:28.270
to a world of happiness for you.

1:01:02.680 --> 1:01:03.720
Blood?

1:01:04.010 --> 1:01:05.590
Why is he here?

1:01:06.100 --> 1:01:08.220
Blood, wait for me!

1:01:14.690 --> 1:01:16.020
Where am I?

1:01:16.020 --> 1:01:17.520
What's going on?

1:01:17.520 --> 1:01:20.070
This is the circus, Miss.

1:01:20.070 --> 1:01:21.280
Circus?

1:01:21.280 --> 1:01:23.030
Isn't this the amusement park?

1:01:23.030 --> 1:01:27.200
Yes, but to come in here, you need a special ticket.

1:01:27.200 --> 1:01:29.240
So, let's see your ticket.

1:01:29.240 --> 1:01:31.160
I don't have one...

1:01:31.160 --> 1:01:32.080
Huh?

1:01:32.080 --> 1:01:33.210
Yes,

1:01:33.750 --> 1:01:35.960
you have a ticket.

1:01:35.960 --> 1:01:38.380
Come right on in.

1:01:38.380 --> 1:01:39.420
Alice!

1:01:39.880 --> 1:01:43.760
You shouldn't wander around here alone. It's dangerous.

1:01:45.760 --> 1:01:49.220
But Boris, I have to look for my vial.

1:01:49.220 --> 1:01:51.890
Vial? You don't need to look for it.

1:01:51.890 --> 1:01:53.980
But if I can't find it...

1:01:53.980 --> 1:01:57.690
Whether you find it or not, you always have your heart.

1:02:02.070 --> 1:02:05.950
For you, the key is always there to drink.

1:02:47.450 --> 1:02:49.870
Are you lost? Want to go home?

1:02:49.870 --> 1:02:52.120
Where will you go? Where will you return to?

1:02:52.120 --> 1:02:54.540
Where are you going? Where do you want to go?

1:02:53.990 --> 1:02:57.620
Do you want to go on? Want to go back?

1:02:57.620 --> 1:03:01.670
There are many paths for me to take, but I can only choose one.

1:03:03.090 --> 1:03:05.050
I must return to my world.

1:03:05.460 --> 1:03:08.050
Isn't that the right thing to do?

1:03:20.520 --> 1:03:22.570
If I lost my balance, I would have fallen...

1:03:27.360 --> 1:03:28.900
How grave.

1:03:29.240 --> 1:03:32.660
You would have died if you fell from the edge.

1:03:32.660 --> 1:03:34.160
Of course I would!

1:03:34.160 --> 1:03:35.950
It's not that easy to choose!

1:03:35.950 --> 1:03:39.500
It's only a choice that will decide whether you live or die.

1:03:40.500 --> 1:03:42.290
No need to be so serious.

1:03:42.290 --> 1:03:43.590
Don't mock me!

1:03:43.590 --> 1:03:45.420
I was just interested.

1:03:45.420 --> 1:03:48.590
Interested in what path an overly serious girl like you would take...

1:03:49.970 --> 1:03:52.680
What choice will you make,

1:03:52.680 --> 1:03:54.720
Outsider Alice?

1:03:58.140 --> 1:04:00.310
The path I choose is...

1:04:25.210 --> 1:04:26.710
Wh-Where am I?

1:04:33.930 --> 1:04:36.260
Hey, it's Alice!

1:04:37.350 --> 1:04:40.100
What's wrong? Why are you turning away?

1:04:40.100 --> 1:04:43.940
It's me! Oh, maybe you can't recognize me.

1:04:45.940 --> 1:04:47.150
Ace?

1:04:47.150 --> 1:04:48.530
Yep, that's me.

1:04:48.530 --> 1:04:49.860
Don't be scared!

1:04:51.070 --> 1:04:52.740
Don't come near me!

1:04:52.740 --> 1:04:55.410
Huh? Why are you backing away?

1:04:55.410 --> 1:04:58.450
I'm no stranger to you.

1:04:58.450 --> 1:04:59.750
You scared?

1:05:00.200 --> 1:05:01.710
Don't run away...

1:05:02.790 --> 1:05:06.500
It's ungentlemanly to cause trouble for a lady.

1:05:06.500 --> 1:05:09.050
I wasn't causing her trouble.

1:05:09.050 --> 1:05:11.010
I haven't even done anything yet.

1:05:11.010 --> 1:05:12.800
"Yet", you say...

1:05:12.800 --> 1:05:16.100
You haven't done anything, but she is afraid of you.

1:05:16.100 --> 1:05:18.890
You might do something to her.

1:05:20.220 --> 1:05:23.230
Is that right? Are you afraid of me?

1:05:23.230 --> 1:05:25.060
I warned you not to scare her.

1:05:25.900 --> 1:05:29.610
But... I'm not the only one she runs away from.

1:05:30.030 --> 1:05:33.110
I don't go about things like you do.

1:05:33.110 --> 1:05:35.740
Oh? So you'd let her escape?

1:05:35.740 --> 1:05:37.490
How unlike a mafioso.

1:05:38.200 --> 1:05:39.450
Not at all.

1:05:39.790 --> 1:05:41.750
Gentlemen just know when to quit.

1:05:41.750 --> 1:05:42.960
I won't quit.

1:05:42.960 --> 1:05:45.960
Because I'm no gentleman—I'm a knave!

1:05:54.430 --> 1:05:55.680
Blood...

1:05:55.680 --> 1:05:56.800
Stay back.

1:05:56.800 --> 1:05:57.720
But...

1:05:58.100 --> 1:06:01.810
Yes, Alice, just stay back.

1:06:01.810 --> 1:06:03.100
You'll only get hurt!

1:06:03.100 --> 1:06:05.810
Even though you tell me to, I can't just stay back!

1:06:05.810 --> 1:06:07.900
Oh, is that so?

1:06:07.900 --> 1:06:09.440
Then <i>I'll</i> stay back.

1:06:19.830 --> 1:06:21.540
What a rotten stench.

1:06:21.540 --> 1:06:26.000
Well, it would be weird if this world had anything good in it!

1:06:42.430 --> 1:06:43.680
It won't budge!

1:06:50.270 --> 1:06:53.280
Hey, can you release me?

1:06:53.610 --> 1:06:55.440
Huh? Why?

1:06:55.440 --> 1:06:57.610
Because this is wrong.

1:06:57.610 --> 1:06:59.910
I'm chained to a target!

1:06:59.910 --> 1:07:01.530
There's nothing wrong with that.

1:07:01.530 --> 1:07:03.620
You are the target!

1:07:03.620 --> 1:07:08.580
Yeah! You're the target now, so there's nothing wrong with chaining you up.

1:07:08.580 --> 1:07:10.880
Wh-What are you doing?!

1:07:10.880 --> 1:07:13.460
You can't use a person as a target!

1:07:14.090 --> 1:07:16.170
Sure we can!

1:07:16.170 --> 1:07:18.260
This is a circus!

1:07:19.340 --> 1:07:21.930
That's right! This is a circus!

1:07:22.720 --> 1:07:24.140
It's a circus!

1:07:26.390 --> 1:07:27.560
Stop!

1:07:30.440 --> 1:07:32.020
You threw them...

1:07:32.020 --> 1:07:34.860
Of course! We're knife-throwers!

1:07:34.860 --> 1:07:38.490
Yeah! If we didn't throw knives, we wouldn't be knife-throwers!

1:07:39.860 --> 1:07:41.820
S-Stop it!

1:07:41.820 --> 1:07:44.200
I'm not a circus act!

1:07:44.580 --> 1:07:48.500
But once you're in the ring, you become part of an act!

1:07:48.500 --> 1:07:49.620
Exactly!

1:07:51.500 --> 1:07:53.170
Please stop!

1:07:53.170 --> 1:07:54.590
I'm bleeding!

1:07:54.960 --> 1:07:58.010
We can't. The circus isn't over yet!

1:08:01.590 --> 1:08:04.600
This fun game isn't over until we hit you!

1:08:13.520 --> 1:08:14.570
Blood!

1:08:18.110 --> 1:08:21.410
A wound of honor! I give up.

1:08:21.410 --> 1:08:23.780
You're like a knight, Hatter.

1:08:23.780 --> 1:08:25.830
Ace, you stop, too!

1:08:25.830 --> 1:08:29.830
That's no fun. I finally got to battle him!

1:08:29.830 --> 1:08:31.580
We don't need to stop.

1:08:35.710 --> 1:08:37.460
Stop it! Stop!

1:08:37.460 --> 1:08:38.340
Certainly not.

1:08:38.920 --> 1:08:42.590
Perhaps you didn't hear the lady's wish.

1:08:48.640 --> 1:08:50.600
No! Don't destroy us!

1:08:54.400 --> 1:08:56.650
It's my time now.

1:08:56.650 --> 1:08:58.230
No! Save us!

1:08:58.230 --> 1:09:00.030
D-Don't do it, Blood.

1:09:13.750 --> 1:09:15.830
Still want to go, Knave of Hearts?

1:09:15.830 --> 1:09:16.920
Wha—?

1:09:20.590 --> 1:09:21.590
Well...

1:09:21.590 --> 1:09:22.630
What?

1:09:22.630 --> 1:09:27.550
Well... doing this makes me the bad guy, right?

1:09:27.550 --> 1:09:28.470
Huh?

1:09:28.470 --> 1:09:30.140
What are you on about?

1:09:30.600 --> 1:09:35.100
It's fine if I'm not a gentleman, but I don't wanna be the bad guy.

1:09:35.100 --> 1:09:37.020
Because I'm a knave.

1:09:37.020 --> 1:09:37.980
Huh?!

1:09:40.190 --> 1:09:42.150
See ya, then, Alice.

1:09:47.280 --> 1:09:49.870
Wh-What <i>is</i> he?

1:09:49.870 --> 1:09:50.870
Who knows?

1:09:50.870 --> 1:09:54.370
He didn't know that he was playing the villain.

1:09:56.120 --> 1:09:57.460
That looks bad.

1:09:58.460 --> 1:09:59.920
It's just a scratch.

1:09:59.920 --> 1:10:01.130
How?

1:10:02.050 --> 1:10:03.760
It will heal quickly.

1:10:03.760 --> 1:10:04.970
Besides that...

1:10:14.690 --> 1:10:18.020
It's strange to see you outside.

1:10:18.020 --> 1:10:19.860
Only because it's night.

1:10:19.860 --> 1:10:22.860
But it wasn't night when you left, was it?

1:10:25.610 --> 1:10:26.860
Shall we return?

1:10:28.570 --> 1:10:29.740
Return?

1:10:29.740 --> 1:10:30.660
Yes.

1:10:30.660 --> 1:10:32.330
Return to the mansion.

1:10:39.540 --> 1:10:43.460
When I first came to this world, he gave me his hand.

1:10:43.460 --> 1:10:45.800
This is... where our path splits.

1:10:54.100 --> 1:10:55.310
Alice...

1:10:56.020 --> 1:10:57.810
Please don't go home.

1:10:58.810 --> 1:11:00.020
Stay here...

1:11:01.110 --> 1:11:03.860
You'll always wake from a dream, Alice.

1:11:05.820 --> 1:11:10.200
Which path will you take? It's up to you to decide.

1:11:10.200 --> 1:11:14.620
Even if you don't, life will go on. You shouldn't rush it.

1:11:57.910 --> 1:12:00.120
Welcome home, Alice.

1:12:00.870 --> 1:12:06.920
sabitsuku furubita neji wo

1:12:00.870 --> 1:12:06.920
The creak of spinning springs,

1:12:06.920 --> 1:12:12.930
mawaseba kishinda oto

1:12:06.920 --> 1:12:12.930
Old and rusted together

1:12:12.930 --> 1:12:18.930
itsukara uchisuterareta ka

1:12:12.930 --> 1:12:18.930
When did you stop using them?

1:12:18.930 --> 1:12:24.770
kioku mo sepia ni kawaru

1:12:18.930 --> 1:12:24.770
Even your memory has turned sepia

1:12:24.770 --> 1:12:30.900
hisometa te kara niji iro ni kaete

1:12:24.770 --> 1:12:30.900
It changed to rainbow with that hidden hand

1:12:30.900 --> 1:12:36.160
kaado fusete kirifuda wa kakusu

1:12:30.900 --> 1:12:36.160
Flip the cards, hide your trump

1:12:36.160 --> 1:12:42.790
toranpu no you kaze ga sarau

1:12:36.160 --> 1:12:42.790
Like in a card game, the wind takes all

1:12:42.790 --> 1:12:47.960
suuji wo otte ana ni hanaru

1:12:42.790 --> 1:12:47.960
And soon the numbers will end in the hole

1:12:47.960 --> 1:12:53.890
heishitachi ni oitaterare

1:12:47.960 --> 1:12:53.890
Leave behind all the soldiers

1:12:53.890 --> 1:13:00.020
shiro usagi wa mitsukaranai

1:12:53.890 --> 1:13:00.020
You won't find the white rabbit

1:13:00.020 --> 1:13:06.360
namae yonde hinto wa suuji no angou

1:13:00.020 --> 1:13:06.360
Call the name, the hint is a numerical code

1:13:06.360 --> 1:13:13.320
chikazuku taimu rimitto

1:13:06.360 --> 1:13:13.320
The time limit is drawing near

1:13:27.960 --> 1:13:33.760
doko made ochiteiku no ka

1:13:27.960 --> 1:13:33.760
How far will you fall?

1:13:33.760 --> 1:13:39.970
shaffuru kurikaesu

1:13:33.760 --> 1:13:39.970
Keep shuffling

1:13:39.970 --> 1:13:45.770
kakumei wo okoseba gyakuten

1:13:39.970 --> 1:13:45.770
Incite a revolution for change

1:13:45.770 --> 1:13:51.940
subete wo hirugaese

1:13:45.770 --> 1:13:51.940
That will flip everything over

1:13:51.940 --> 1:13:57.780
onaji kao ni shinkei suriherashi

1:13:51.940 --> 1:13:57.780
A familiar face lowers your defenses

1:13:57.780 --> 1:14:03.210
haato no furue yubi ni mo tsutawaru

1:13:57.780 --> 1:14:03.210
Your wavering heart makes even your fingers tremble

1:14:03.210 --> 1:14:09.800
kouun sutete daiya wo motome

1:14:03.210 --> 1:14:09.800
Never mind luck, go for the gold

1:14:09.800 --> 1:14:14.840
subete wo tsukami aka ni somaru

1:14:09.800 --> 1:14:14.840
Keep it all and be stained in red

1:14:14.840 --> 1:14:21.010
yami ni magire tsuzuku saiban

1:14:14.840 --> 1:14:21.010
The trial continues through the confusion of the dark

1:14:21.010 --> 1:14:27.020
joou no tsue mujou ni furuu

1:14:21.010 --> 1:14:27.020
The queen wields her sceptre in her cruelty

1:14:27.020 --> 1:14:33.530
nagetsuke atte amasa hajikeru kaori

1:14:27.020 --> 1:14:33.530
She tosses it aside and out bursts a sweet scent

1:14:33.530 --> 1:14:39.620
tokei fumitsubushita

1:14:33.530 --> 1:14:39.620
On the trampled clocks

1:14:41.030 --> 1:14:45.250
kazoku no shouzou omori de katamuku tenbinza

1:14:41.030 --> 1:14:45.250
The weight of a family portrait tipping Libra's scales

1:14:52.250 --> 1:14:58.340
tsuki to taiyou wo sakasa ni mawasu

1:14:52.250 --> 1:14:58.340
The sun and moon move in reverse

1:14:58.340 --> 1:15:04.430
akarui yoru ni

1:14:58.340 --> 1:15:04.430
To bring the bright night

1:15:04.430 --> 1:15:10.110
chizu wa yabure yaku ni tatazu

1:15:04.430 --> 1:15:10.110
The map is torn and useless

1:15:10.110 --> 1:15:16.490
kemuri fukikake nemuke sasou

1:15:10.110 --> 1:15:16.490
Blow smoke, the seduction of sleepiness

1:15:16.490 --> 1:15:23.030
boushi no soko saraeba uso ga afuredasu

1:15:16.490 --> 1:15:23.030
Take the out bottom of the hat and out pours lies

1:15:23.030 --> 1:15:28.830
garasu tatakiwarou

1:15:23.030 --> 1:15:28.830
Shatter the glass

1:15:28.830 --> 1:15:35.800
akaku nijimu sekai

1:15:28.830 --> 1:15:35.800
Of the world smeared in red

1:17:04.340 --> 1:17:06.260
Now that I think about it...

1:17:06.260 --> 1:17:07.220
What?

1:17:07.220 --> 1:17:12.520
Didn't Alice lose something important? A vial or something?

1:17:12.520 --> 1:17:15.610
Where did it end up anyway?

1:17:17.440 --> 1:17:18.650
Who knows?

1:17:18.650 --> 1:17:24.570
I don't know who did it, but anyone who takes something so important to a girl is terrible.

1:17:24.570 --> 1:17:25.870
A real lowlife.

1:17:25.870 --> 1:17:27.080
I suppose.

1:17:27.660 --> 1:17:29.240
But whoever did it

1:17:29.740 --> 1:17:30.870
is the villain.

1:17:31.910 --> 1:17:33.420
Hey, Blood...

1:17:33.790 --> 1:17:36.580
The reason Alice was so invested in this place

1:17:36.580 --> 1:17:39.920
was because she lost some kind of important vial.

1:17:39.920 --> 1:17:42.380
Oh, a vial?

1:17:42.380 --> 1:17:43.970
What vial is that?

1:17:43.970 --> 1:17:45.760
I dunno, but...

1:17:45.760 --> 1:17:49.390
She was saying that she can't go back home without it.

1:17:49.390 --> 1:17:51.850
Hm... that's a shame.

1:17:51.850 --> 1:17:54.350
Yeah, I feel for her.

1:17:54.350 --> 1:17:58.980
Unfortunately, I don't know anything about her vial.

1:17:58.980 --> 1:18:01.860
All I have is this rubbish I found.

1:18:03.360 --> 1:18:06.320
The lady says the strangest things.

1:18:06.320 --> 1:18:10.740
How can she not go back home when she is already home?

1:18:10.740 --> 1:18:12.120
Home, huh?

1:18:12.660 --> 1:18:14.330
You're right.

1:18:14.330 --> 1:18:16.370
She doesn't need this piece of junk!

1:18:40.730 --> 1:18:45.900
fukai yami ochiteikeba chigau sekai

1:18:40.730 --> 1:18:45.900
If you fall into the darkness,
you'll end up in another world

1:18:45.900 --> 1:18:51.030
miruku iro kiri no naka ni yobareteru ki ga suru

1:18:45.900 --> 1:18:51.030
You'll feel as though the milky-
white mist is calling to you

1:18:51.030 --> 1:18:56.290
dare no mono? mekki ga hage iro aseteku

1:18:51.030 --> 1:18:56.290
Whose is this?
Break the façade and fade away

1:18:56.290 --> 1:19:01.800
watashi nara takaramono wa dare nimo yuzuranai

1:18:56.290 --> 1:19:01.800
I won't give my treasure to anyone

1:19:11.810 --> 1:19:17.060
mukashi mita omochabako ni niteru ki ga suru

1:19:11.810 --> 1:19:17.060
It looks like a toybox I saw a long time ago

1:19:17.060 --> 1:19:22.860
heitai ni garasu no shiro moroi merengetachi

1:19:17.060 --> 1:19:22.860
With a soldiers in
a glass castle and brittle merengues

1:19:22.860 --> 1:19:28.070
garasu no kutsu wo migaite mo muda ne

1:19:22.860 --> 1:19:28.070
Don't bother polishing your glass slippers

1:19:28.070 --> 1:19:33.910
oujisama wa koko ni wa konai

1:19:28.070 --> 1:19:33.910
No prince will come for you here

1:19:40.460 --> 1:19:44.300
ochiteyuku dake no wandawarudo

1:19:40.460 --> 1:19:44.300
A wonderworld where all you do is fall

1:19:44.300 --> 1:19:48.170
wasurerareteku yuuenchi

1:19:44.300 --> 1:19:48.170
The amusement park you'll soon forget

1:19:48.170 --> 1:19:50.590
kirei na mono wa yume

1:19:48.170 --> 1:19:50.590
Everything beautiful is a dream

1:19:50.590 --> 1:19:55.600
biizu no yubiwa wa itsuka wa chigireru

1:19:50.590 --> 1:19:55.600
The bead ring will eventually be torn apart

1:19:55.600 --> 1:20:02.230
watashi no omocha yo kodomo no mama isasete

1:19:55.600 --> 1:20:02.230
With all my toys, just let me stay a child

1:20:02.230 --> 1:20:07.280
torokeru wana ni deguchi ga mienai

1:20:02.230 --> 1:20:07.280
It's an enchanting trap with no escape in sight

1:20:07.280 --> 1:20:12.410
usagi ga warau wandarando

1:20:07.280 --> 1:20:12.410
Where the rabbit laughs—Wonderland

1:21:51.380 --> 1:21:56.590
machiawase matedo konai himitsu no hito

1:21:51.380 --> 1:21:56.590
Waiting for a secret person who won't come

1:21:56.590 --> 1:22:02.430
garasu dama shabon dama hajikete kieru awa

1:21:56.590 --> 1:22:02.430
Glass beads and soap suds
pop and vanish like bubbles

1:22:02.430 --> 1:22:07.810
mamotte hoshii kara yakusoku shinai de

1:22:02.430 --> 1:22:07.810
You should keep your promises,
so make none to me

1:22:07.810 --> 1:22:12.900
uso wo tsukasetakunai wa

1:22:07.810 --> 1:22:12.900
I don't want you to lie to me

1:22:12.900 --> 1:22:17.950
waratta hoshii no uso demo ii kara

1:22:12.900 --> 1:22:17.950
I want you to laugh, even if it's not real

1:22:17.950 --> 1:22:24.000
guruguru mawaru meiro mitai

1:22:17.950 --> 1:22:24.000
Like a labyrinth where we keep going in circles

1:22:31.500 --> 1:22:35.550
sotto nozoku dake no wandawarudo

1:22:31.500 --> 1:22:35.550
A wonderworld where you only get a peek

1:22:35.550 --> 1:22:39.470
niji no hashi wa fumenai kara

1:22:35.550 --> 1:22:39.470
Because you can't cross the rainbow bridge

1:22:39.470 --> 1:22:41.970
kirei na mono wa yume

1:22:39.470 --> 1:22:41.970
Everything beautiful is a dream

1:22:41.970 --> 1:22:47.020
nidoto hirakanai ochakai ga owaru

1:22:41.970 --> 1:22:47.020
The tea party is over,
and you'll never have one again

1:22:47.020 --> 1:22:53.530
utage ga owareba anata mo kieteshimau

1:22:47.020 --> 1:22:53.530
Once the feast is over, you will disappear, too

1:22:53.530 --> 1:22:58.570
yuganda kagi de tobira wo tojita

1:22:53.530 --> 1:22:58.570
The door was locked with a crooked key

1:22:58.570 --> 1:23:03.910
usagi ga haneru wandarando

1:22:58.570 --> 1:23:03.910
Where the rabbit hops—Wonderland

1:23:03.910 --> 1:23:09.080
torokeru wana ni deguchi ga mienai

1:23:03.910 --> 1:23:09.080
It's an enchanting trap with no escape in sight

1:23:09.080 --> 1:23:14.210
usagi ga warau wandarando

1:23:09.080 --> 1:23:14.210
Where the rabbit laughs—Wonderland
